@startuml
title Role-based Authorization (SecurityConfig.securityFilterChain)
hide footbox
actor Client
participant SecurityConfig
participant JwtAuthenticationFilter as JwtFilter
participant AuthController
participant UserController
participant TodoController

Client -> SecurityConfig: HTTP request (Authorization: Bearer token, optional)
SecurityConfig -> JwtFilter: doFilter (added before UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter)
JwtFilter --> SecurityConfig: Authentication is set (valid token and ACTIVE user)\nor left empty (see JWT Filter diagram)

note over SecurityConfig: authorizeHttpRequests rules are matched in declaration order.\nhasRole("X") checks the authority "ROLE_X".

alt Path matches /api/auth/** (permitAll)
    SecurityConfig -> AuthController: allow request
    AuthController --> Client: Login response
else Path matches /api/admin/** (hasRole ADMIN)
    alt No Authentication (missing, invalid or expired token, or inactive user)
        SecurityConfig --> Client: 401 Unauthorized (authenticationEntryPoint)
    else Authentication has ROLE_ADMIN
        SecurityConfig -> UserController: allow request
        UserController --> Client: Admin User response
    else Authentication without ROLE_ADMIN (for example ROLE_USER)
        SecurityConfig --> Client: 403 Forbidden (accessDeniedHandler)
    end
else Path matches /api/todos/** (hasRole USER)
    alt No Authentication
        SecurityConfig --> Client: 401 Unauthorized (authenticationEntryPoint)
    else Authentication has ROLE_USER
        SecurityConfig -> TodoController: allow request
        TodoController --> Client: Todo response
    else Authentication without ROLE_USER (for example ROLE_ADMIN)
        SecurityConfig --> Client: 403 Forbidden (accessDeniedHandler)
    end
else Any other path (anyRequest().authenticated())
    alt No Authentication
        SecurityConfig --> Client: 401 Unauthorized (authenticationEntryPoint)
    else Authenticated with any role
        SecurityConfig --> Client: allow request
    end
end
@enduml